  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 16

Iteration 15 already existed when this session said \"next\". It is the amu
pin, not call-clobber. This file does not overwrite it. Iteration 8 left a
closer: a function with calls and control flow still took all-vreg. That is
the only measured gap this loop still owned after the leaf closed inside
noise.

## What landed

`kotoba-mir` `7f7c55691697ba25abf6d732870a159433ce1fab` (ADR 0012): the linear
scanner accepts calls. Non-leaf pool is scratch then preserved. Values whose
last use follows a call prefer a preserved register at definition. Remaining
live caller-saved values are stored at their definition, which dominates both
arms. Call-site moves of live-across values into preserved are not used —
they are CFG-unsafe. Straight-line callers keep ADR 0006 `allocate-call-live`.
Leftover pressure still fails into all-vreg. Successful scan declares
`:call-live`.

`kotoba-native` `f07d260e79e0ab5c5c01df9b85808624b5c86498` pins that mir.
West pins: kotoba-mir `91b24675`, kotoba-native `47b76357`. amu's native pin
is unchanged.

Mir 42 tests / 985 assertions. Native 168 tests / 2199 assertions. Both green
before merge.

## Break / unbreak (AArch64, pin f07d260e)

compile-gmir on the four fixtures. Helper `step` is a leaf (`:allocator`, 0
slots) in every case.

| kernel | live | path | policy | slots | insns | kernel bytes | n=7 oracle |
|---|---:|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `kernel_call` | 8 chained | straight | `:call-live` | 8 | 48 | 240 | 6210431302 |
| `kernel_call_branch` | 8 chained | one `if` | `:call-live` | 1 | 46 | 248 | 6210431302 |
| `kernel_call_deep` | 24 | straight | `:call-live` | 24 | 191 | 808 | 21432348 |
| `kernel_call_deep_branch` | 24 | one `if` | `:call-live` | **17** | **168** | **652** | 21432348 |

Iteration 8's conservative path on the 24-live branch was **99 slots, 325
insns, 1344 B**. The same source now takes the linear scanner and does not
store every SSA value. x86-64 agrees on policy: 24-live branch is `:call-live`
at 20 slots / 172 insns, not all-vreg.

The 24-live branch is now *smaller* than its straight-line twin. Straight-line
still uses ADR 0006, which materializes every live-across value into a slot.
The CFG path prefers preserved registers at definition. That difference is
real and is not this iteration's ranking question. The ranking question was
whether the extra `if` paid all-vreg. It does not.

## Oracle, offset, execute

Twins agree with the interpreter at n=7 and n=200. extract-native / KIR
export offset for `kernel` is **52** on this pin (iteration 8 saw 72). Timing
offset 0 still runs `step`; `step(7)` is 337898.

`compile-kir-module` wrote the AArch64 bytes; `kexe-benchmark` (isa hoisted)
ran them at offset 52. n=7, 1 call after 1 warmup:

| kernel | result |
|---|---:|
| `kernel_call` | 6210431302 |
| `kernel_call_branch` | 6210431302 |
| `kernel_call_deep` | 21432348 |
| `kernel_call_deep_branch` | 21432348 |

Offset 0 on every module returns 337898 (`step(7)`). The 24-live branch's
taken arm is the same arithmetic as the straight-line twin, executed, not
only encoded. x86-64 encodings were produced in the same dump (24-live
branch 1010 B, `:call-live`, 20 slots); this host does not run them natively.

loadavg was `{ 47 39 28 }`. Elapsed nanoseconds on a 1-call sample is not a
ranking. No perfgate claim.

## What this is not

- Not a leaf rematch. Iteration 14's refusal stands.
- Not a timed ranking of the 33% tax. The tax's *cause* is gone from the
  encodings. Sealing a ns/call number needs a quiet host and
  `perfgate.core/qualify`.
- Not an amu pin bump. Same rule as 11-14: encodings are not a timed win on
  a published export.
- Not fused-srem, extra MOV, FMA, PGO, or a kototama optimizer.
- Not a call-site move of live-across values into preserved.

## Next

